    "result_text": "AcceptanceTest is the only test class, and it passes. The build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the GOLD membership tier rule. When an owner's household (owners sharing the same `householdId`) reaches 3 or more members after a create, the owner's `membershipTier` is `GOLD`; otherwise the existing SILVER/BRONZE rules apply.\n\nChanges, following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions and the existing `namesakeCount` pattern:\n\n1. **`Owner` model** \u2014 added a persisted `householdSize` field (`household_size` column) with getter/setter, mirroring `namesakeCount`.\n\n2. **Schema** \u2014 added the `household_size` column to all four `schema.sql` files (hsqldb used by tests, plus h2/mysql/postgres for parity).\n\n3. **`CountHouseholdMembers`** (new function step) \u2014 counts owners sharing the new owner's `householdId` plus one for the not-yet-saved new owner, and stores it as `householdSize`. A non-shared owner (`householdId == null`) is a household of one. It runs right after `AssignHousehold`, which sets and back-fills the shared `householdId`, so the count is accurate.\n\n4. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired `countHouseholdMembers` into the pipeline between `assignHousehold` and `assignCustomerCode`, under the same `transaction` governance.\n\n5. **`OwnerMapper.membershipTier`** \u2014 returns `GOLD` first when `householdSize >= 3`, otherwise falls through to the unchanged SILVER/BRONZE logic.\n\nThe tier is derived at response-mapping time from the persisted entity, so a fresh `GET /api/owners/{id}` (as the test does) correctly reports `GOLD` for the third household member. `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.",
